  "question": {
    "text": "The B-H curve for a ferromagnet is shown in the figure. The ferromagnet is placed inside a long solenoid with 1000 turns/cm.. The current that should be passed in the solenoid to demagnetize the ferromagnet completely is:\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/iamdkDz5SswpvEK4gja5hdFHCCGN3_D6WgX1w5NzXBo.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Xjx5Q",
      "text": "\n$2 \\mathrm{~mA}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Li7WL",
      "text": "\n$1 \\mathrm{~mA}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ptpku",
      "text": "\n$40 \\mu \\mathrm{A}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "5FOJv",
      "text": "\n$20 \\mu \\mathrm{A}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given Number of turns, $\\mathrm{n}=1000$ turns $/ \\mathrm{cm}=1000 \\times 100$ turns $/ \\mathrm{m}$ Coercivity of ferromagnet, $\\mathrm{H}=100 \\mathrm{~A} / \\mathrm{m}$ Current to demagnetise the ferromagnet, $\\mathrm{I}=?$\nUsing, $\\mathrm{H}=\\mathrm{nI}$\nor, $\\quad 100=10^5 \\times \\mathrm{I}$\n$\\therefore \\quad \\mathrm{I}=\\frac{100}{10^5}=1 \\mathrm{~mA}$",
    "image": null
  },
